Q: C# Data generator for Oracle: ORA-26010 A: <p>Some 5 years later, using NET10 and you still need to use DataTables to insert bulk into Oracle. I had the same problem and solved it by adding ColumMappings.</p>
<pre><code>  using var bulkCopy = new OracleBulkCopy(connection)
  {
      DestinationTableName = table.TableName,
      BatchSize = 1000,
  };
  bulkCopy.ColumnMappings.Add(new OracleBulkCopyColumnMapping(0, 1));
  bulkCopy.ColumnMappings.Add(new OracleBulkCopyColumnMapping(1, 2));
  bulkCopy.ColumnMappings.Add(new OracleBulkCopyColumnMapping(2, 3));
  bulkCopy.ColumnMappings.Add(new OracleBulkCopyColumnMapping(3, 4));
  bulkCopy.ColumnMappings.Add(new OracleBulkCopyColumnMapping(4, 5));
  bulkCopy.ColumnMappings.Add(new OracleBulkCopyColumnMapping(5, 6));
  bulkCopy.ColumnMappings.Add(new OracleBulkCopyColumnMapping(6, 7));
</code></pre>
<p>Since I skip the ID column, I have to shift all the other columns. Never mind that the column names match.</p>
<p>And then I found a simpler solution. Define the column, but don't give it a value. Like this:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code> var table = new DataTable(&quot;Gevallen&quot;);
 table.Columns.Add(&quot;Id&quot;, typeof(long));
 table.Columns.Add(&quot;Registratienummer&quot;, typeof(long));
 table.Columns.Add(&quot;Bsn&quot;, typeof(string));

var row = table.NewRow();
row[&quot;Bsn&quot;] = g.Bsn;
row[&quot;Registratienummer&quot;] = g.Registratienummer;
</code></pre>

Q: Microsoft Graph Page Iterator async/ non-async lambda function A: <p>The issue is that <code>graphClient.Groups[id].Members.GetAsync</code> returns the <code>DirectoryObjectCollectionResponse</code> and your page iterator expects the <code>UserCollectionResponse</code>.</p>
<p>You can use casting on members and return only users who are the members of a group.</p>
<p>Use <code>graphClient.Groups[id].Members.GraphUser.GetAsync</code>.</p>
<pre><code>var members = await graphClient.Groups[id].Members.GraphUser.GetAsync(requestConfiguration =&gt;
           {
               requestConfiguration.QueryParameters.Select = [   
                   &quot;userPrincipalName&quot;, &quot;displayName&quot;, &quot;mail&quot;,
                   &quot;givenName&quot;, &quot;surname&quot;
               ];
           });

           var iterator = PageIterator&lt;User, UserCollectionResponse&gt;.CreatePageIterator(
               graphClient,
               members,
               (user) =&gt;
               {
                   if (allMembers.ContainsKey(user.Id))
                       return true;
                   var nameParts = user.UserPrincipalName.Split('@');
                   EmployeeViewModel employee = new EmployeeViewModel
                   {
                      /* Creation logic */
                   };
                   allMembers.TryAdd(user.Id, employee);
                   return true;
               },
               (req) =&gt;
               {
                   return req;
               });
           await iterator.IterateAsync();
</code></pre>
<p>One note...you can't return photo for multiple users. You can retrieve photo only for one user at a time.</p>
